      "title": "Apply to Vice President for Enrollment Management and Marketing",
      "description": "Apply to Vice President for Enrollment Management and Marketing | Warner Pacific University Visit our website View job listing Apply to Vice President for Enrollment Management and Marketing Summary Description: Reporting to the President and serving as a member of the Executive Cabinet, the Vice President for Enrollment Management and Marketing provides visionary leadership for the University's comprehensive enrollment enterprise. The Vice President is responsible for developing and executing an integrated enrollment strategy that advances the University's mission, strengthens financial sustainability, and supports long-term institutional growth. The Vice President provides executive leadership for undergraduate, graduate, professional, adult, and online enrollment; admissions; student financial services; enrollment marketing and communications; and strategic enrollment operations. The University's marketing and communications functions report to Enrollment Management and serve as strategic partners in achieving enrollment objectives. The Vice President provides executive oversight for institutional marketing, brand management, digital marketing, enrollment communications, content strategy, website strategy, social media, and market positioning to ensure a consistent, mission-centered institutional voice while supporting student recruitment across all academic programs. As the University's chief enrollment strategist, the Vice President partners with Academic Affairs, Student Life, Finance, Athletics, Advancement, and Information Technology to create a seamless, student-centered enrollment experience from prospect through graduation. The Vice President uses data-informed decision making, market intelligence, and collaborative leadership to position Warner Pacific University for sustainable enrollment growth while advancing its Christ-centered mission, commitment to student success, and service to diverse communities. Primary Job Duties: Strategic Enrollment Leadership Serve as the University's chief enrollment strategist leading the University's comprehensive Strategic Enrollment Management (SEM/SEP) planning process. Develop multi-year enrollment, retention, and net tuition revenue goals that support the University's financial sustainability and mission. Partner with Academic Affairs to assess market demand for existing and proposed academic programs and recommend opportunities for enrollment growth. Enrollment Strategy & Operations Provide executive leadership and direct supervision of Admissions, Student Financial Services and Enrollment Marketing and Communications. Lead the development and execution of comprehensive recruitment strategies for all student populations, including first-time freshmen, transfer, graduate, professional, adult, online, and international students, as applicable. Oversee the development and implementation of annual recruitment plans with measurable objectives, timelines, and performance metrics. Collaborate with Student Success, Academic Affairs, and other campus partners to improve student persistence, retention, and successful transition throughout the student lifecycle. Oversee and direct recruitment initiatives executed by contracting vendor partners. Financial Aid & Net Revenue Strategy Develop and oversee comprehensive financial aid leveraging strategies that optimize enrollment, student access, and institutional financial sustainability while ensuring compliance with all federal, state, and institutional regulations. Lead institutional scholarship and discounting strategies to maximize enrollment outcomes and achieve approved net tuition revenue goals. Collaborate with the Finance Office to develop enrollment forecasts, tuition revenue projections, financial models, and annual budget assumptions. Monitor key enrollment and financial performance indicators, including discount rates, yield, net tuition revenue, and return on investment for enrollment initiatives. Marketing & Communications Provide executive leadership for the University's integrated marketing and communications strategy in support of enrollment growth and institutional visibility. Oversee enrollment marketing, digital marketing, website strategy, enrollment communications, content development, brand management, and market positioning across all student populations. Ensure marketing initiatives effectively communicate Warner Pacific University's Christ-centered mission, academic strengths, and value proposition to prospective students and families. Evaluate marketing effectiveness through performance metrics, market research, and return-on-investment analyses, making strategic adjustments to maximize enrollment outcomes. Data, Technology & Analytics Provide executive oversight for the University's enrollment technology to develop and monitor executive dashboards and key performance indicators that support enrollment forecasting, recruitment performance, financial aid optimization, and student success initiatives. Champion the effective use of technology, automation, artificial intelligence, and data-informed decision-making to improve enrollment effectiveness and operational efficiency. Leadership & Collaboration Recruit, develop, mentor, and evaluate a high-performing enrollment leadership team committed to collaboration, innovation, accountability, and continuous improvement. Partner collaboratively with Academic Affairs, Student Life, Finance, Advancement, Athletics, Information Technology, and other campus leaders to achieve institutional enrollment and student success goals. Lead organizational change initiatives that improve enrollment processes, enhance operational effectiveness, and strengthen cross-functional collaboration. Prepare and manage division budgets and ensure responsible stewardship of institutional resources in support of enrollment priorities. External Relations & Institutional Leadership Serve as a member of the President's Executive Cabinet and provide regular reports to senior leadership and the Board of Trustees regarding progress toward enrollment, retention, financial aid, and net tuition revenue goals. Provide high level briefings to keep leadership informed of market trends and related directional decisions. Represent Warner Pacific University within churches, schools, community colleges, employers, professional organizations, and community partners to strengthen institutional relationships and enrollment opportunities. Demonstrate a commitment to a Christian liberal arts education by upholding the mission of the University and abiding by the Employment Standards and Lifestyle Agreement. Warner Pacific is affiliated with the Church of God (Anderson, Indiana), while fostering an inclusive and welcoming campus community that values diversity, equity, belonging and service. Perform other duties as assigned by the President. Minimum Qualifications: Minimum of eight years of progressively responsible leadership experience in higher education enrollment management, including minimum five years of experience at a supervisory level. Master’s degree from an accredited institution required, doctorate or other terminal degree preferred. Experience leading comprehensive enrollment management functions, including admissions, recruitment, financial aid, enrollment marketing, and strategic enrollment planning. Ability to lead organizational change, build high-performing teams, and foster collaboration across academic and administrative divisions. Strong financial management skills, including budget development, resource allocation, and strategic planning. Excellent communication, presentation, and relationship-building skills with the ability to effectively engage trustees, faculty, staff, students, donors, churches, community partners, and external stakeholders. Preferred Qualifications: Earned doctorate (Ed.D, Ph.D. or other terminal degree) in higher education, business, leadership, marketing or a related field. Experience serving as a senior-level enrollment executive. Experience developing and implementing strategic enrollment plans that align with institutional mission and financial sustainability. Expertise in financial aid leveraging, scholarship optimization, tuition discount management, and enrollment forecasting. Experience leading integrated marketing and enrollment communication strategies, including digital marketing, brand management, and prospective student engagement. Experience utilizing CRM systems (preferably Slate), enrollment technologies, and analytics tools to support recruitment, communication, and operational effectiveness. Ellucian Colleague experience desirable. Physical Demands – Work Environment: The position is located in a typical office environment.  Professional/business attire is required. Warner Pacific University’s Mission: Warner Pacific is a Christ-centered, urban, diverse, minority-serving, Hispanic-serving, liberal arts University dedicated to providing students with an education that prepares them to engage actively in a constantly changing world. Our hiring practices reflect our missional commitment to being a Christ-centered institution. Warner Pacific University’s Commitment to Diversity: Warner Pacific University is an Equal Opportunity Employer that seeks a diverse workforce of committed Christians from all racial, ethnic, and socio-economic backgrounds. Warner Pacific University is committed to hiring staff and faculty with an intentionality that demonstrates the importance of having an employee community that reflects the racial and ethnic diversity of the students we serve. Employment and Lifestyle Standards: Warner Pacific is a Christ-centered urban liberal arts University dedicated to providing students from diverse backgrounds an education that prepares them to engage actively in a constantly changing world. The University was founded in 1937 by the Church of God (Anderson, Indiana). Central to Warner Pacific’s identity as a Christ-centered higher education institution is the policy of hiring persons whose personal and professional lives reflect: 1.   A belief in the deity of and commitment to Jesus Christ and the Christian faith, as interpreted through the historic witness of Scripture and the continuing ministry of the Holy Spirit. 2.  The practice of following Christ through day-to-day personal lifestyle choices. 3.  A vitality of Christian experience maturing in insight and application and appreciative of differing viewpoints. 4.  A commitment to life-long learning and service through personal and professional development. 5.  For teaching faculty, the expression of artful teaching, based on mastery of relevant subject matter and in an environment of purposeful and rigorous inquiry amongst a community of scholars who support one another. 6. A capability, by temperament, preparation, and will, to support students as they confront the intellectual, social, physical, emotional, and spiritual challenges of their lives. 7.   A sensitivity to and support for the mission, core themes, vision, values, ethos and traditions of the Warner Pacific University community. 8. A commitment to teaching and serving in harmony with the doctrines of the Holy Bible. Employee Agreement: Mission-based hiring is of critical importance to Warner Pacific University. Employees are expected to demonstrate and articulate a vital Christian faith and to live in a manner consistent with a Christ-centered lifestyle as informed by the Scriptures of the New Testament. Warner Pacific’s students, faculty and staff are expected to foster an environment of mutual respect and accountability, to care for the personal dignity of others and to exercise integrity in their conduct and communication. The University environment is expected to be free from discrimination and harassment (including bullying). When an individual’s behavior has direct implications for others and/or the well-being of the University community, there may be cause for institutional involvement, regardless of where the situation occurs. Warner Pacific University desires to provide a safe and healthy environment for staff, faculty, students, visitors and guests. Therefore, smoking is not permitted on University property, in its vehicles, or at any University sponsored event. The use of illegal drugs or non-prescribed controlled substances is strictly prohibited. Use of alcoholic beverages or tobacco products is strictly prohibited on Warner Pacific University campuses. Equal Employment Opportunity: Warner Pacific provides equal opportunity for employment and advancement for all employees and applicants regardless of race, color, sex, gender, national origin, citizenship status, disability, age, genetic information, status with regard to public assistance, veteran status and any other status protected by laws and regulations to which Warner Pacific is subject.  All employment decisions, including hiring, promotions, compensation, benefits, transfers, and terminations are made in a manner that does not discriminate against individuals in the categories discussed above.  Because Warner Pacific is a Christian liberal arts University, the University exercises its legal right to hire Christian employees to fulfill its mission and purpose. Click “Apply Now” to complete the online application, and submit the following: Application Cover Letter Resume ** NOTE: All job offers are contingent upon successfully passing a background check and completing all required paperwork. Thank You for Your Interest in a Career at Warner Pacific University! Warner Pacific provides equal opportunity for employment and advancement for all employees and applicants regardless of race, color, sex, gender, national origin, citizenship status, disability, age, genetic information, status with regard to public assistance, veteran status and any other status protected by laws and regulations to which Warner Pacific is subject.  All employment decisions, including hiring, promotions, compensation, benefits, transfers, and terminations are made in a manner that does not discriminate against individuals in the categories discussed above.  Because Warner Pacific is a Christian University, the University exercises its legal right to hire Christian employees to fulfill its mission and purpose. Instructions: Before completing this application, please read the below Employment Standards and Lifestyle Agreement. Then complete the entire application. Employment and Lifestyle Standards: Warner Pacific is a Christ-centered urban liberal arts University dedicated to providing students from diverse backgrounds an education that prepares them to engage actively in a constantly changing world. The University was founded in 1937 by the Church of God (Anderson, Indiana). Central to Warner Pacific’s identity as a Christ-centered higher education institution is the policy of hiring persons whose personal and professional lives reflect: 1.   A belief in the deity of and commitment to Jesus Christ and the Christian faith, as interpreted through the historic witness of Scripture and the continuing ministry of the Holy Spirit. 2.  The practice of following Christ through day-to-day personal lifestyle choices. 3.  A vitality of Christian experience maturing in insight and application and appreciative of differing viewpoints. 4.  A commitment to life-long learning and service through personal and professional development. 5.  For teaching faculty, the expression of artful teaching, based on mastery of relevant subject matter and in an environment of purposeful and rigorous inquiry amongst a community of scholars who support one another. 6. A capability, by temperament, preparation, and will, to support students as they confront the intellectual, social, physical, emotional, and spiritual challenges of their lives. 7.   A sensitivity to and support for the mission, core themes, vision, values, ethos and traditions of the Warner Pacific University community. 8. A commitment to teaching and serving in harmony with the doctrines of the Holy Bible. Thank you for your interest in Warner Pacific University. Note:  Windows Explorer is no longer a supported browser.  Please use either Google Chrome or Firefox when submitting your application and use a laptop or desktop.  Other devices such as iPhone, tablets, iPad, Notebook, etc. do not always submit correctly. Personal Information Upload Resume * Drop files here, paste or browse Upload Cover Letter * Drop files here, paste or browse First Name * Last Name * Email * Address * City * State * Zip Code * Phone * Mobile Phone What are your salary requirements? * Education High School and Location (City/State) * Undergraduate Education -College, Location (City/State) Undergraduate Degree Rec'd - Field of Study Graduate Education - College, Location (City/State) Graduate Degree Rec'd - Field of Study Additional College Education -  College, Location (City/State) Additional Degrees Rec'd - Field of Study Work Experience 1. Most Recent Employer and Location (city/state) * 1.  Job Title * 1. Supervisor Name and Phone # * 1. Dates of Employment (Month/Year) * 1. Reason for Leaving Position * 2. Employment History - Employer, Location (city/state) * 2.  Job Title * 2. Dates of Employment (Month/Year) * 2. Reason for Leaving Position * 3. Employment History - Employer, Location (city/state) * 3.  Job Title * 3. Dates of Employment (Month/Year) * 3. Reason for Leaving Position * May we contact your current employer? * Yes No Level of expertise in MS Word, PowerPoint, Excel, & Outlook Very Experienced Some Experience Knowledge Need Practice Honors, Awards, Professional Memberships & Distinctions Additional experience or training related to this position Please describe opportunities you have had to work with diverse populations and in multicultural contexts. * References 1. Provide 3 professional references: Name, Relationship/Position, Phone * 2. Professional References: Name, Relationship/Position, Phone * 3. Professional References:  Name, Relationship/Position, Phone * Statement of Faith Indicate the church you attend and the denomination * Include level of activity with your church * Very Active Moderately Active Inactive Briefly describe your Statement of Christian Faith * Belief + Action = Faith.\r\n\r\nMany of us claim having religion as faith, but what do our actions show?  Tell us about what you believe and how you pursue what you believe. Please provide a detailed statement articulating the ways in which faith informs your understanding of your vocation and this opportunity at Warner Pacific. * Explain how your faith shapes how you think about your life’s purpose/work (your “vocation”), and\r\nwhy this specific role or opportunity at Warner Pacific matters to you. Voluntary Information The following questions are to insure EEOC compliance and are strictly voluntary. We maintain this data for EEOC inquiries and to assist in any discrimination investigations by the federal, state, and local governments. Gender Male Female X Ethnicity American Indian or Alaskan Native Asian Hispanic or Latino Black or African American White Native Hawaiian or other Pacific Islander Two or more races Authorization By submitting this application with your electronic signature, you are agreeing to the following statements:\n\nI verify that all information provided during the application process, including this application and any attached information is completely accurate and acknowledge that inaccurate information or material omissions could disqualify me from consideration for the position or result in termination if I am hired. I authorize Warner Pacific University to verify the information provided and to conduct reference checks. I authorize any references to give you any and all information concerning my previous employment and any pertinent information they may have, personal or otherwise, and I release from all liability or responsibility the University, it's ag If hired, can you provide proof that you are lawfully entitled to work in the U.S. on an unrestricted basis? * Yes No Where did you hear about this position? * Warner Pacific University's website Craigslist Oregonian/OregonLive Indeed HigherEd Jobs CCCU HERC Partners in Diversity Hispanic Outlook Latinos in Higher Education Journal of Black Issues in Higher Education Native Americans in Higher Education Asians in Higher Education A friend or relative referred me Another source Today's Date * Electronic Signature - please type your legal name. * Next Page Page 1 of 5 Submit Application Powered by"
